        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 1. Employees who have been released from work and are then called back to work outside of their regular shift schedule shall be guaranteed a minimum of three hours' pay. Employees receiving call time assignments shall be credited for beginning work when they arrive at the work site. Call time shall be paid for at whatever rate is appropriate. Employees will be permitted to leave the work site when the work assignment that is the reason for the call time is completed unless the employee's scheduled work shift has commenced. There shall be no duplication of hours or pay.",
